WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.850
A nerve impulse speeds along an
axon until it reaches the very end.

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:09.480
There, it meets a gap it cannot
jump: the synaptic cleft.

3
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:13.910
And signals cross it in one
direction only, never backwards.

4
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.780
So if the impulse cannot jump the
gap, how does the message get across?

5
00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.510
In this mission, you'll
zoom into a synapse,

6
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.890
where one nerve cell meets the next.

7
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.940
Then you'll see the same kind of junction
linking a nerve cell to an effector,

8
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.400
such as a muscle.

9
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:34.770
Your mission: find out how the message
gets across a gap the impulse cannot jump.
